; beancount reads a transaction with more than two strings to its end
; before it rejects it, so its amounts count towards display precision: USD
; is written with two digits twice below, in the dropped transaction, and
; without digits twice.
2020-01-01 open Assets:Stock
2020-01-01 open Expenses:B
2020-01-01 open Equity:E

2020-01-04 * "kept"
  Assets:Stock  3 STK {{10 USD}}
  Equity:E

2020-01-05 * "one" "two" "three"
  Expenses:B   1.00 USD
  Equity:E    -1.00 USD

2020-01-06 * "kept too"
  Expenses:B   2 USD
  Equity:E
